WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.660
Marvel fans have been waiting years for a
Black Widow solo movie, and from the first

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:10.100
trailer it looks like we'll be getting some
awesome action scenes, and fantastic new characters

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.209
joining the MCU, including a brand new villain,
Taskmaster.

00:00:14.209 --> 00:00:18.230
And with Marvel's history of twist reveals
for their villains and the actor playing Taskmaster

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:23.800
currently a secret, fans have already begun
to speculate about who's really beneath the

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:24.800
helmet.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.599
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm going to explain all the hidden

00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:32.410
clues in the Black Widow teaser that reveal
Taskmaster's true identity and the secret

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:33.770
twist in the movie.

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:38.900
Also, keep watching for details of an incredible
thousand-dollar gift-card giveaway with bonus

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.790
goodies, all thanks to this video's sponsor
Marvel Collect!

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:42.790
By Topps.

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:47.590
Quick warning, there will, of course, be speculation
and potential spoilers for Black Widow.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:51.770
As a super-spy movie, Black Widow will be
full of characters double-crossing each other

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:54.050
and hiding secret intentions.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:57.752
And when Taskmaster is revealed, it will likely
be someone that's already close to Natasha

00:00:57.752 --> 00:01:02.040
in some way in order to magnify the impact
of that twist.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:07.000
Potential candidates include Florence Pugh's
Yelena, Rachel Weisz's Melina, and O.T.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.420
Fagbenle's mysterious character Mason.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:14.119
I'm going to say straight away that Red Guardian
won't be Taskmaster because he's clearly fighting

00:01:14.119 --> 00:01:15.420
the villain in this scene.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:19.179
However, there is another character from Natasha's
past who we also need to consider.

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:24.179
There's a popular theory that Taskmaster is
actually Hawkeye in disguise.

00:01:24.179 --> 00:01:27.920
I'm going to explain why that's highly unlikely,
but first let's review the evidence.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:32.289
The theory suggests the villain's skilled
bow and arrow technique fits perfectly with

00:01:32.289 --> 00:01:34.819
Clint Barton's expertise as an archer.

00:01:34.819 --> 00:01:39.439
If this twist were true, it would be particularly
shocking because Nat and Clint have been great

00:01:39.439 --> 00:01:44.030
friends throughout their time together in
the MCU, despite being on opposite sides for

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:46.469
a while during Civil War:
"We're still friends aren't we?"

00:01:46.469 --> 00:01:48.399
"Depends on how hard you hit me."

00:01:48.399 --> 00:01:53.100
And – spoilers for Avengers: Endgame – when
they go to Vormir to recover the Soul Stone,

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:58.130
Nat even sacrifices herself so Clint can live
and get his own Disney+ TV show.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:02.469
So, their friendship and Natasha's future
sacrifice would make Hawkeye being the twist

00:02:02.469 --> 00:02:07.209
villain in her own solo movie feel especially
cruel and improbable.

00:02:07.209 --> 00:02:11.700
The only real way it could make sense is if
this moment is a flashback to the time that

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.370
Clint came after Natasha on SHIELD's orders.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:16.939
"I got on S.H.I.E.L.D.'s radar in a bad way.

00:02:16.939 --> 00:02:18.850
Agent Barton was sent to kill me.

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:20.220
He made a different call."

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:24.709
It would be pretty weird though if Clint suited
up as Taskmaster for this mission unless he'd

00:02:24.709 --> 00:02:29.650
somehow gone rogue or was being mind-controlled
by someone else like he was by Loki in the

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:31.349
first Avengers movie.

00:02:31.349 --> 00:02:35.630
That all feels like a big stretch though and
the final nail-in-the-coffin for this theory

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:40.620
could be that Taskmaster draws the bow with
his right hand whereas the MCU's Clint is

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:42.930
left-handed when he uses the bow.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:47.120
What's probably going on in this scene is
that Taskmaster has copied Hawkeye's archery

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:51.430
skills from a previous encounter with him
and is now using them against Natasha.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:56.250
That's because Taskmaster has the power of
photographic reflexes meaning he can mimic

00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:00.579
and duplicate the moves, tricks and skills
of anyone he observes.

00:03:00.579 --> 00:03:04.890
Another possibility is that this is the Budapest
event that's been referenced so many times

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:10.099
in the Infinity Saga and that Taskmaster is
fighting Clint and imitating him in the moment.

00:03:10.099 --> 00:03:12.409
"Just like Budapest all over again."

00:03:12.409 --> 00:03:14.680
"You and I remember Budapest very differently."

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:16.980
"..long way from Budapest."

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:21.099
For our next Taskmaster candidate we need
to take a look at new Black Widow character,

00:03:21.099 --> 00:03:26.019
Melina Vostokoff played by Rachel Weisz who
intriguingly revealed some juicy details about

00:03:26.019 --> 00:03:28.330
Melina during an interview at Comic Con.

