00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:12.400
OK, back to Taskmaster's secret identity.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:17.000
Speaking to EW, Rachel Weisz explained that
Melina is a seasoned assassin who's been through

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:22.370
the Black Widow programme five times, and
that she "was deeply involved in a scientific

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:23.370
experiment."

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:27.030
Weisz then said she couldn't talk about that
any further, and this itself means that her

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:31.540
character Melina is very likely to factor
into one of the movie's major twists.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:36.580
In the comics, Melina Vostokoff is a former
Russian agent also known as Iron Maiden, who

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:39.919
becomes resentful of Black Widow and attempts
to kill her.

00:05:39.919 --> 00:05:44.910
In the Black Widow trailer, Melina's nefarious
intentions towards Natasha aren't made obvious

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:49.580
and instead we see her with Nat, Yelena and
Red Guardian, reuniting for a meal as if they

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:52.069
are old friends:
"Family..

00:05:52.069 --> 00:05:54.550
Back together again."

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:57.030
"You got fat."

00:05:57.030 --> 00:06:01.820
But Melina's somewhat uncomfortable looks
in that scene suggest she could be hiding

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:02.820
something.

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:07.190
The "scientific experiment" that Rachel Weisz
mentioned might be the creation of David Harbour's

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:11.949
Red Guardian, who in the comics was the Soviet
Union's answer to Captain America.

00:06:11.949 --> 00:06:15.270
Or it could be Melina's creation of her own
Iron Maiden suit.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:20.139
However, I have a feeling that Melina could
actually be responsible for creating Taskmaster

00:06:20.139 --> 00:06:24.259
and that the "scientific experiment" is what
ends up giving the villain its powers of mimicry

00:06:24.259 --> 00:06:25.259
and duplication.

00:06:25.259 --> 00:06:30.319
Interestingly, duplication and mirroring appear
to be a theme in the Black Widow movie that

00:06:30.319 --> 00:06:32.720
goes beyond Taskmaster.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:35.840
For example, when we see Yelena and Natasha
fight each other, they mirror and duplicate

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:37.760
the other's postures and moves.

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:41.980
Obviously, they were also trained under the
same system but this symbolic mirroring seems

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:44.919
to be something the film is pushing thematically
as well.

00:06:44.919 --> 00:06:49.389
Here we see all the Black Widow operatives
moving and turning in unison.

00:06:49.389 --> 00:06:54.120
And during this aerial freefall, these three
mercs are each performing the same motion,

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:56.090
reminding me a bit of clones.

00:06:56.090 --> 00:07:00.379
The real question to ask ourselves here is
whether Melina will be the person inside the

00:07:00.379 --> 00:07:04.099
Taskmaster costume or did she experiment on
somebody else?

00:07:04.099 --> 00:07:08.690
Well, there's actually a sneaky clue that
can help answer this in one of the other Taskmaster

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:10.139
scenes from the trailer.

00:07:10.139 --> 00:07:13.629
When we see the villain go up against Red
Guardian in a one-on-one fight, there's an

00:07:13.629 --> 00:07:18.470
interesting visual perspective on how the
two characters compare in terms of height.

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:22.840
If we draw a line, we can see there's only
a slight difference in height, with Taskmaster

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:25.930
appearing to be just a little shorter than
Red Guardian.

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:32.169
According to IMDB, Rachel Weisz who plays
Melina is 5ft 6 inches tall, whereas David

00:07:32.169 --> 00:07:37.509
Harbour, aka Red Guardian, is almost nine
inches taller at nearly 6ft 3.

00:07:37.509 --> 00:07:41.240
That's a much bigger height difference than
this fight scene would suggest.

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:45.490
Admittedly, both characters aren't standing
straight so we can't measure the height difference

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:50.720
exactly, but they both have their knees bent
by roughly the same amount, and neither one

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:55.220
is wearing significantly thicker boots that
would boost their height.

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:58.949
It's unlikely therefore that this is Melina
in the Taskmaster outfit.

00:07:58.949 --> 00:08:04.689
Now, there is actually another main Black
Widow cast member who would fit in that costume

00:08:04.689 --> 00:08:06.099
and that's actor O.T.

00:08:06.099 --> 00:08:11.819
Fagbenle who's 6ft exactly, making him just
3 inches shorter than David Harbour which,

00:08:11.819 --> 00:08:14.949
when we look at this picture, seems to be
about the right amount.

00:08:14.949 --> 00:08:19.470
Fagbenle, best known for his work in The Handmaid's
Tale, is playing a character called Mason

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:20.470
in Black Widow.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:25.439
In the cast interview with EW, he described
Mason as "a fixer, […] the guy who can get

00:08:25.439 --> 00:08:29.830
things done if you're a spy or superhero and
need a little bit of extra help."

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:34.520
The actor also revealed that Mason "has a
bit of a complex relationship" with Natasha

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:36.760
and a romantic interest in her.

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:40.610
Mason's name or Nat's prior relationship with
him has never been mentioned or discussed

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:45.190
in previous MCU movies, which could mean the
filmmakers will use that to show that their

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:49.250
relationship didn't go well and Natasha never
wanted to bring it up.

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:53.660
In the comics, Mason worked for SHIELD, but
he also had a freelance background working

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:57.570
as a covert operative where he was simply
known as "The Agent".

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:02.000
Given Black Widow is a super-spy movie, it's
also quite possible that Mason is some kind

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:06.579
of double-agent who works both for SHIELD
and the Russians or Melina specifically.

00:09:06.579 --> 00:09:12.100
I think it's interesting that Fagbenle chooses
not to reveal which side Mason works for in

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:17.510
the interview with EW, especially as he exchanges
a subtle glance with Rachel Weisz while describing

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:19.200
Mason's role in the film.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:20.470
"He's like a fixer..

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:24.290
He's kind of the guy who can get things done..
..if you're a spy or a superhero and you need

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:25.490
a bit of extra help.

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:26.670
Ahhm.. sort you out..

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:27.670
..I'm still..

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:28.790
I work.. all the time.."

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:33.170
And notice how Rachel Weisz smiles knowingly
to herself when the interviewer initially

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:35.350
asks O.T. to talk about his character.

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:38.230
"So O.T. tell us a bit about.. the character
that you play."

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:39.510
Oh yeah, I play erm..

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:41.010
Mason and er.."

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:45.740
Given all this and how little has been revealed
about O.T.'s role in Black Widow, all clues

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:48.700
currently point to him being Taskmaster.

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:53.750
Of course, some fans have speculated that
Yelena could be masquerading as Taskmaster.

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:58.880
If we go by the height theory though, then
she'd be the least likely candidate, as Florence

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:04.970
Pugh at around 5ft 4 is almost a whole foot
shorter than Red Guardian actor David Harbour.

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:09.380
Additionally, given Natasha's fate in Endgame,
this film will probably serve as a way to

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:14.160
set up a new Black Widow character for future
MCU movies and it looks like Yelena is the

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:16.540
most likely candidate for that right now.

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:20.480
So, who do you think Taskmaster really is
underneath the helmet?

